# Frontend Chat Integration Guide - Lazy Chat Creation

## Summary of Backend Changes

Chat is now created **only when the first message is sent**, not when opening a conversation. This prevents empty chats.

---

## 1. `join_chat` Event (Changed)

### Emit (unchanged)
```javascript
socket.emit("join_chat", { 
    recipientId: "user_id_here",
    jobId: "optional_job_id"  // optional
});
```

### Response - `chat_joined` (NEW FORMAT)

**If chat exists:**
```javascript
{
    chatId: "676abc123...",
    chat: { participants: [...], messages: [...], ... },
    isNewChat: false,
    recipientOnline: true
}
```

**If no chat exists (new conversation):**
```javascript
{
    chatId: null,               // No chat yet!
    isNewChat: true,
    recipient: {
        _id: "...",
        firstName: "John",
        lastName: "Doe",
        profilePhoto: "...",
        email: "..."
    },
    recipientOnline: true,
    jobId: "optional_job_id"
}
```

### Frontend Handler Example
```javascript
socket.on("chat_joined", (data) => {
    if (data.isNewChat) {
        // No chat exists - show empty conversation UI
        setChatId(null);
        setRecipient(data.recipient);
        setMessages([]);
        setJobId(data.jobId);
    } else {
        // Existing chat
        setChatId(data.chatId);
        setMessages(data.chat.messages || []);
    }
    setRecipientOnline(data.recipientOnline);
});
```

---

## 2. `send_message` Event (Changed)

### Emit - For NEW chat (no chatId)
```javascript
socket.emit("send_message", {
    recipientId: "user_id_here",  // Required for new chats
    jobId: "optional_job_id",     // Optional
    content: "Hello!",
    messageType: "text",          // Optional
    attachments: [],              // Optional
    relatedJob: "optional_job_id" // Optional
});
```

### Emit - For EXISTING chat (has chatId)
```javascript
socket.emit("send_message", {
    chatId: "chat_id_here",
    content: "Hello!",
    messageType: "text",
    attachments: []
});
```

### Response - `message_sent` (NEW FORMAT)
```javascript
{
    chatId: "676abc123...",
    message: { _id: "...", content: "Hello!", ... },
    isNewChat: true,              // NEW: Indicates chat was just created
    chat: { ... }                 // NEW: Full chat object (only if isNewChat)
}
```

### Frontend Handler Example
```javascript
socket.on("message_sent", (data) => {
    if (data.isNewChat) {
        // Chat was just created! Update the chatId
        setChatId(data.chatId);
        setChat(data.chat);
    }
    addMessage(data.message);
});
```

---

## 3. Sending Messages - Complete Flow

```javascript
const sendMessage = () => {
    const messageData = {
        content: inputText,
        messageType: "text",
        attachments: [],
    };

    if (chatId) {
        // Existing chat - use chatId
        messageData.chatId = chatId;
    } else {
        // New chat - use recipientId
        messageData.recipientId = recipientId;
        messageData.jobId = jobId;  // if applicable
    }

    socket.emit("send_message", messageData);
};
```

---

## 4. Quick Reference

| Scenario | Use | Result |
|----------|-----|--------|
| Open new conversation | `join_chat` with recipientId | Returns recipient info, `chatId: null` |
| Send first message | `send_message` with recipientId | Creates chat, returns `isNewChat: true` |
| Send subsequent messages | `send_message` with chatId | Normal message send |
| Open existing conversation | `join_chat` with recipientId | Returns existing chat |

---

## 5. State Management Suggestion

```javascript
const [chatId, setChatId] = useState(null);
const [recipientId, setRecipientId] = useState(null);
const [recipient, setRecipient] = useState(null);
const [messages, setMessages] = useState([]);
const [isNewChat, setIsNewChat] = useState(false);

// When opening a conversation
const openChat = (userId) => {
    setRecipientId(userId);
    socket.emit("join_chat", { recipientId: userId });
};

// When receiving join response
socket.on("chat_joined", (data) => {
    setIsNewChat(data.isNewChat);
    if (data.isNewChat) {
        setChatId(null);
        setRecipient(data.recipient);
    } else {
        setChatId(data.chatId);
    }
});

// When message is sent
socket.on("message_sent", (data) => {
    if (data.isNewChat) {
        setChatId(data.chatId);
        setIsNewChat(false);
    }
});
```
